---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetricCard from "../../components/MetricCard.astro";
import ResultTable from "../../components/ResultTable.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/Figure.astro";
import AssignmentIdentity from "../../components/AssignmentIdentity.astro";
import { external } from "../../data/site";
import { percent, readCsv } from "../../lib/csv";
import eda from "../../../assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/eda_samples.png";
import curves from "../../../assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/all_models_curves.png";
import confusion from "../../../assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/cm_cnn.png";
import robustness from "../../../assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/robustness_curve.png";

const results = readCsv("assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/comparison_summary.csv", ["Model", "Parameters", "Test_Acc", "Test_Macro_F1", "Train_Time_s"]);
const budget = readCsv("assignments/assignment-1/source/results/fashion_mnist/matched_budget_summary.csv", ["Model", "Parameters", "Test_Acc", "Test_Macro_F1"]);
---
<BaseLayout title="Assignment 1" description="Fashion-MNIST architecture comparison for CO3133 Assignment 1." current="a1">
  <section class="shell page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Assignment 1 · Foundations</p><div class="page-status"><span class="status status-complete">Implementation and all final deliverables available</span></div><h1>Foundations of Deep Learning Pipelines and Architectures</h1><p class="page-lead">From linear models to modern sequence models: a controlled Fashion-MNIST comparison of representation, capacity, accuracy, and robustness.</p></section>
  <AssignmentIdentity />
  <section class="shell"><div class="metric-grid"><MetricCard label="Best model" value="91.22%" detail="CNN test accuracy" accent={true} /><MetricCard label="Best Macro-F1" value="91.20%" detail="CNN on the official test split" /><MetricCard label="Fair split" value="50k / 10k / 10k" detail="Train / validation / official test · seed 42" /></div></section>
  <section class="shell article-layout"><article><section class="article-section"><h2>Problem statement</h2><p>Classify 28×28 grayscale Fashion-MNIST images into ten classes. The main comparison implements and trains Linear, MLP, CNN, LSTM, GRU, and patch-based Transformer classifiers under a common split and evaluation protocol.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Dataset description and EDA</h2><p>The source uses 50,000 training images, 10,000 validation images, and the official 10,000-image test set. Inputs are normalized with mean and standard deviation 0.5; EDA confirms the image shape, class coverage, and representative samples.</p><div class="result-grid"><Figure src={eda} alt="Fashion-MNIST representative samples arranged by class" caption="Representative Fashion-MNIST samples used during exploratory analysis." /><Figure src={curves} alt="Training and validation curves for all Assignment 1 models" caption="Learning curves across the completed main model comparison." /></div></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Methodology</h2><p>All main models use cross-entropy loss, Adam optimization, fixed seed 42, and model selection by validation Macro-F1. The study contrasts flattened-pixel, convolutional, row-sequence, and patch-token representations.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Experimental setup</h2><p>Runs use batch size 64, ten epochs, CUDA when available, and deterministic seed handling across Python, NumPy, PyTorch, and CUDA. Checkpoints are selected on validation Macro-F1 and then evaluated once on the official test set.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Results</h2><p>The CNN is the strongest completed main model on Fashion-MNIST. The full, traceable comparison below is generated from the repository result CSV.</p><ResultTable caption="Fashion-MNIST main comparison" rows={results} columns={[{key:"Model",label:"Model"},{key:"Parameters",label:"Parameters"},{key:"Test_Acc",label:"Test accuracy",format:percent},{key:"Test_Macro_F1",label:"Macro-F1",format:percent},{key:"Train_Time_s",label:"Train time",format:(value) => `${value}s`}]} /></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Comparison and discussion</h2><p>The matched-budget experiment isolates representational choices at approximately 105K parameters. CNN remains strongest on accuracy and Macro-F1, while the Transformer incurs the highest observed training and inference cost in this setup.</p><ResultTable caption="Matched-parameter-budget comparison" rows={budget} columns={[{key:"Model",label:"Model"},{key:"Parameters",label:"Parameters"},{key:"Test_Acc",label:"Test accuracy",format:percent},{key:"Test_Macro_F1",label:"Macro-F1",format:percent}]} /></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Error analysis</h2><p>Confusion matrices, representative predictions, saliency maps, and controlled noise/occlusion tests expose where representations differ. The final report consolidates these findings into a written error taxonomy with representative examples.</p><div class="result-grid"><Figure src={confusion} alt="CNN confusion matrix on Fashion-MNIST test set" caption="CNN confusion matrix on the official Fashion-MNIST test split." /><Figure src={robustness} alt="Model accuracy under increasing Gaussian noise" caption="Robustness under increasing Gaussian-noise perturbation." /></div></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Limitations and conclusion</h2><p>Results are limited to the stated training budget and Fashion-MNIST primary benchmark. The source, result artifacts, report, slides, and presentation video are published for review and reproduction.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Assignment-specific AI Usage Disclosure</h2><p>Four documented Google Gemini uses supported visualization, CSV, saliency, robustness, and report-formatting work. One OpenAI Codex use supported final-report consistency and publication review. Each output was checked against documentation, generated artifacts, and committed result CSVs. <a href={external.a1Ai}>Read the complete Assignment 1 log.</a></p></section></article><aside class="side-stack"><section class="resource-card"><p class="eyebrow">Resources</p><h2>Deliverables</h2><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Source}><span>Source code</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Readme}><span>Reproduction & checkpoints</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Results}><span>All result artifacts</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Report}><span>Final report</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Slides}><span>Presentation slides</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Video}><span>Presentation video</span><b>Watch ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a1Ai}><span>AI disclosure</span><b>Open ↗</b></a></section></aside></section>
</BaseLayout>
